  "hints": [
    "Equal values can be used multiple times when there are multiple occurrences, but equivalent choices at one depth should not repeat.",
    "Sort the input and skip equal adjacent candidates only among siblings in the same recursive call.",
    "Save the current subset. For i from start, skip when i>start and values[i]==values[i-1]; otherwise choose i and recurse from i+1.",
    "Do not globally discard duplicates: [2,2] and [2] are distinct valid subsets."
  ],
  "editorial": "Sort to place equal values together. Within one call, selecting a later copy as the first new choice would duplicate the branch from the earlier copy, so skip it. Once a value has been selected, the next recursive level may select another occurrence. This permits every valid multiplicity while producing each multiset exactly once. The independent oracle enumerates all occurrence masks and deduplicates their sorted tuples.",
